Step-7  Go to aws console select ec2 instance  and go inside the security group in bottom 

			open all traffic of ports    32000-35000  for everywhere 
			
Step-8  Now again login on Ec2 instance and try to install nginx 

			dnf install nginx -y
			
Step-9  Start , enable and check status of nginx 

		systemctl start nginx
		systemctl enable nginx 
		systemctl status nginx 

Step-10   Now  go inside the /etc/nginx/conf.d/

and create new file named as  ecblb.conf and put following code inside it 
( Please remember to change below IP according to your containers )



upstream backend_ecbserver {            #  This perform load balancing
    server 172.17.0.2:80;
    server 172.17.0.3:80;
    server 172.17.0.4:80;
    server 172.17.0.5:80;
}

server {
    listen 80;
    server_name _;

    location / {
        proxy_pass http://backend_ecbserver;    # This perform reverse proxy

        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
    }
}



